OR - ALTERNATIVE TEST AT THE CURRENT IF LEVEL

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
OR - ALTERNATIVE TEST AT THE CURRENT IF LEVEL

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

Syntax:
    OR condition [arguments]

Combines the current condition with another test using logical OR. Unlike
a nested IF, it updates the current level. If there is no active IF, it
starts a level.

Example: IF NULL X;OR NULL;ECHO ONE TRUE;FI

The same test availability and access limits as IF apply.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
